# Bash naming

Prefixes match [../cpp/naming.mdc](../cpp/naming.mdc) (same logic, snake_case). `scripts/bash_macros/`, `scripts/bash_bringup/`, `scripts/bash_env/`: [macros.mdc](macros.mdc).

A prefix describes **behavior type**. Use it when it improves readability; otherwise keep a plain verb. Applies to **new code** — do not refactor legacy unless asked.

## Prefixes

| Prefix | Returns | Meaning | Good example | Bad example |
|--------|---------|---------|--------------|-------------|
| `is_` | bool (exit 0/1) | “is X true now?” | `is_wsl()`, `is_broken_local_cmake()` | `is_velocity` returning a number |
| `has_` | bool | “does it exist / is it available?” | `has_config()`, `has_command()` | `has_path` when it returns a path |
| `get_` | a value | read with no state change | `get_project_root()`, `get_host_arch()` | `get_and_source` — side effect |
| `set_` | — | write / configure | `set_workspace_root()`, `set_default_middleware()` | `set_path` when it only reads |
| `try_` | bool | operation that may fail | rare in bash | `try_build` when `build` is always the command |

Private helpers in `scripts/bash_macros/`, `scripts/bash_bringup/`, and `scripts/bash_env/`: `ns::_is_foo` (e.g. `diag::_has_command`, `bringup::_is_sourced`, `env::_init_ros2_env`) — [macros.mdc](macros.mdc). Public commands — core macros (`build`, `cbuild`, `diag`, `load_macros`, `importer`) or any public macro from a subproject bundle — **no** prefix.

## Abbreviations

Keep names short, but spell out words a reader would have to expand. `term` for “terminal”, `cfg` for “config”, `mgr` for “manager” — no. Prefer `diag::_get_terminal_width` over `diag::_get_term_width`. Established acronyms are fine (`ros`, `src`, `uri`, `xml`).
